/target

# Cached raw scrape responses (~60 MB of HTML).
#
# The plan called for committing these as an audit trail, but that is too much
# weight for a git repo. The audit trail that actually matters survives anyway:
# every entry in data/matchups.toml records the per-source values it was blended
# from, so a suspicious number can still be traced back to the site that
# produced it. Re-fetching is one `just ingest --refresh`.
/data/sources/

# Personal match history. Every line is a game somebody actually played, which
# is theirs rather than the repo's, and of no use to a fresh clone. The server
# writes it wherever OVERWATCH_MATCH_LOG points, so a deployment that wants to
# keep results puts them outside the working tree rather than un-ignoring this.
# Comment it out to track your own.
/data/matches.jsonl
